`getUser(session)` returns `session.user`, which is `undefined` for any session without an authenticated user (missing/expired/anonymous session). `login()` then dereferences `.id` on that `undefined` value with no guard — that's the exact `TypeError: cannot read properties of undefined (reading 'id')`. This is the only place in the repo that reads `.id` (confirmed via full-repo grep), so it's the sole source of the crash. It's a pre-existing landmine, not something a specific line changed — the repo has no git history at all (fresh, uncommitted, zero commits), so I can't pin it to a Tuesday diff, but the defect is unambiguous.

